# IoT RF Gateway

ESP32-based LoRa RF Gateway using the AI-Thinker RA-02 (SX1278) module.

The gateway receives LoRa JSON payloads from field devices, validates the device Farm ID, and publishes valid sensor or keepalive data to MQTT.

## Data Flow

```text
LoRa Sensor Device
        ↓
ESP32 + RA-02 RF Gateway
        ↓
MQTT Broker
        ↓
farm/{farm_id}/sensor
farm/{farm_id}/sensor_keepalive
```

## Hardware Required

- ESP32 DevKit
- AI-Thinker RA-02 LoRa module
- 433 MHz LoRa antenna
- Stable 3.3V power supply
- SPI jumper wires

## RA-02 to ESP32 Pin Connection

| RA-02 Pin | ESP32 GPIO | Purpose |
|---|---:|---|
| VCC | 3.3V | Power — do not use 5V |
| GND | GND | Common ground |
| SCK | GPIO 18 | SPI clock |
| MISO | GPIO 19 | SPI data from RA-02 |
| MOSI | GPIO 23 | SPI data to RA-02 |
| NSS / NCS | GPIO 13 | SPI chip select |
| RST | GPIO 27 | RA-02 reset |
| DIO0 | GPIO 26 | LoRa receive interrupt pin |

Unused available ESP32 pins:

```text
GPIO 25
GPIO 33
```

## LoRa Settings

Sender and receiver must use exactly the same settings:

```cpp
#define LORA_FREQUENCY 433000000L
#define LORA_SYNC_WORD 0x34

LoRa.setSpreadingFactor(7);
LoRa.setSignalBandwidth(125000);
LoRa.setCodingRate4(5);
LoRa.enableCrc();
```

Sender transmit power:

```cpp
LoRa.setTxPower(17);
```

## PlatformIO Libraries

Add this to `platformio.ini`:

```ini
lib_deps =
    sandeepmistry/LoRa
    bblanchon/ArduinoJson
```

## Example THC Sensor Payload

```json
{
  "Etemp": 30.4,
  "Humidity": 18.2,
  "CO2": 527,
  "DN": "THC",
  "rack_id": 5,
  "type": "sensor",
  "Device_Id": "IFTHC1230000001",
  "Packet_Id": "0ad4113b-d168-4d53-a32e-88c11d0adb88"
}
```

## Example FWD Water-Level Payload

```json
{
  "DN": "FWD",
  "WaterLevel": 257.137146,
  "Device_Id": "IFFWD1230000001",
  "Packet_Id": "4a34c41b-ee93-4ea3-a870-3f845350a2cb",
  "rack_id": 2,
  "type": "sensor"
}
```

## MQTT Topics

```text
farm/123/sensor
farm/123/sensor_keepalive
farm/123/info
```

## Device ID Format

```text
IF + DN (3 letters) + Farm ID (3 digits) + serial number
```

Example:

```text
IFTHC1230000001
     ^^^
     Farm ID = 123
```

The gateway only publishes a LoRa payload when its parsed Farm ID matches the locally configured `FARM_ID`.

## Build and Upload

```bash
pio run
pio run -t upload
pio device monitor -b 115200
```

## Important Notes

- Connect a proper 433 MHz antenna before transmitting.
- RA-02 requires 3.3V power and logic levels.
- Use `strcmp()` for DN checks, not `DN == "THC"`.
- JSON keys are case-sensitive: `WaterLevel` and `waterLevel` are different.
- Use a unique `Packet_Id` for every sensor packet in production.
- Keep sender and receiver LoRa frequency, sync word, spreading factor, bandwidth, and coding rate identical.